post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
NetControl installed.

1. Enable the service:
     sudo systemctl enable --now netcontrol

2. The first administrator password is written to:
     /var/lib/netcontrol/initial-admin-password.txt
   Read it with:
     sudo cat /var/lib/netcontrol/initial-admin-password.txt
   It is removed after the first administrator login.

3. Local enforcement uses the restricted helper:
     /usr/lib/netcontrol/netcontrol-helper
   The sudoers rule at /etc/sudoers.d/netcontrol allows only the netcontrol
   service user to invoke it. Review it before enabling the service.

4. For remote API access, configure TLS in
   /var/lib/netcontrol/config.toml and set allow_remote = true.
   Never expose the API over plaintext HTTP.

Discovery and monitoring work without the helper. Blocking and bandwidth
enforcement require a configured, authorized gateway.
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  post_install
}

pre_remove() {
  systemctl stop netcontrol.service 2>/dev/null || true
}
